<title>USA: Centralia, Wash. coal-fired power unit seen up Wed.</title>
<headline>Centralia, Wash. coal-fired power unit seen up Wed.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 670 megawatt (MW) unit 2 at the Centralia, Wash., coal-fired power plant is expected to restart by Wednesday, Oct 9, after shutting down Monday for repairs to a tube leak, a spokeswoman for Puget Sound Power and Light Co said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Puget is a minority partner in the Centralia project, which is operated by 47.5-percent owner PacifiCorp.</p>
<p>Centralia's other 670 MW unit was said to be operating normally.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau, + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
